We have a SWXCR controller that is installed on an Alphaserver 1000. We
want to operate it in jbod mode and move some disks to it that are on
other alpha systems and some from some DECstations. The documentation
is very very sparse on how to use this. We used the administration tool
on the ecu disk and the swxcrmgr program and think we have everything
configured properly. We have one disk drive (an rz56) attached to it
for test purposes and the administration software seems to recognize it
just fine. We then booted with the generic kernel and it finds the xcr
controller
                                        Initializing xcr0.  Please wait. 
                                        Initializing xcr0.  Please wait. 
                                        Initializing xcr0.  Please wait. 
                                        Initializing xcr0.  Please wait. 
                                        Initializing xcr0.  Please wait. 
