Is there anyone out ther who knows about the "lpd No such printer OSFQUEUE"
when running Pathworks V 5.0 Lan-Manager server on DEC Unix ?

I cannot find any docs dealing with those hidden funtions. All i figured out
until now is the mechanism, that reproduces the error:

Install P/W server on DEC Unix (no customizations !). Looking at the queues
menu of pwadmin shows OSFQUEUE.

Make any printer connected locally to the Alpha a P/W share.

Look at /etc/printcap: *No* entry named OSFQUEUE, but "lmxnul" and "lmx???"
What the heck are these good for ???

Start a P/W client on a PC and run Windows (3.1 or WfW-Net 3.11, makes no 
difference here). Be sure to connect to one *real* of the printer shares 
mentioned above.

Start up the Print-Manager, it should show "Network error". *At the same
time* the console log of the Alpha (if enabled via "*.debug /dev/console" in
syslog.conf) should display the above eror message concerning OSFQUEUE.


Please help, any suggestions welcome !


A. Schindler  (please E-Mail to schindler@iid.com) 



