: test=O\'Neil
: echo $test | tr '\047' '\047\047'
: O'Neil

: test="John & Martha"
: echo $test | tr '\046' and
: John a Martha

: How can I substitute a single character with several?

Try
test=O\'Neil
echo $test | sed "s/'/''/g"
O''Neil

and
test="John & Martha"
echo "${test}" | sed "s/&/a/g"
John a Martha

