The Alpha port of Linux is now stabilising and the code tree merged
with the standard Linux develpoment tree (at 1.3.30ish). It runs
nicely on Alpha PC64 (Cabriolet) (275Mhz,189 SPECint, 262 SPECfp),
AXPpc/33 (Noname) (166MHz, 94 SPECint, 110 SPECfp) and similar
systems (21066@266Mhz-based for example). No OSF/1 license fee
and less memory/disk hungry than OSF/1. According to a talk from
a hardware DECcie, they not only accept this but are happy with
it (and actively helped Linus with the port) because anything that
sells more Alpha chips is fine by them. I believe that at least
one of {Free,Net}BSD also runs on Alpha. Please don't sink to the
level of going to Windows/NT unless you've considered all other
possibilities ;-)

