Robert> we want to use our 2100 server for SMP with tree CPU's. As far
Robert> as I know is the slowest clock-rate important for the rate of
Robert> the whole system, the other CPU's use this clockrate too, even
Robert> if they are higher rated. We are now using a 190 MHz CPU and
Robert> are thinking about 233 or 250 MHz. Is it possible to replace
Robert> this CPU without any problems ( hardware and software (like
Robert> licenses)).

As far as I know, you cannot mix CPU types in the 2100 series
machines.  If you put a 275 Mhz CPU board in with a 190 Mhz board, bad
things could happen to your system.

Right now, I've seen ads for 190 Mhz CPUs boards for $2700, with SMP
license for Digital Unix.  This is a great way to boost the
performance of an older 2100 4/200 system on the cheap.  No need to
buy the 4/233 or 4/275 or 5/250 boards for lots of bucks.  

For upgrading from a 4/200 to a 4/2xx, then you should be all set.  To
goto the 5/250 board you will need to recompile your kernel and to
install new firmware on your system.  But the rest of your system and
licences won't change.

