X-Deja-AN: 118087554
distribution: world
sender: beb@mpeu28.rosat.mpe-garching.mpg.de (Bernt Christandl)
organization: Rechenzentrum der Max-Planck-Gesellschaft in Garching
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

Hi,

for those of you who are not subscribed to alpha-osf-managers@ornl.gov
(hint hint ;) here is what i've learned this week about tcsh and dxterm
under Digital Unix (V3.0 and V3.2C at least):

I've had the problem that my prompt after starting a dxterm appears only 
after about one minute or two instead of one second or two. 

I was using tcsh, version  ( `echo $version' )

  tcsh 6.05.00 (Cornell) 94/19/06 (alpha-dec-osf1) options 8b,nls,dl,al,rh

and i'm working from an Xterminal (that is: over the net...)


Solutions to that problem are

-> using dec's /usr/bin/csh  (OSF/1 3.0 or DU 3.2C at least)  or

-> using dxterm without `-ls' option  or

-> working directly on the machine without any network being involved  or

-> reconfiguring/remaking tcsh with REMOTEHOST in config_c.h `undef'ed

All solutions worked for me. With the forth one, i've installed the newer
tcsh-6.06 from ftp.deshaw.com in /pub/tcsh and have now version

  tcsh 6.06.00 (Cornell) 1995-05-13 (alpha-dec-osf1) options 8b,nls,dl,al

Note the missing `rh' at the end of the line.

My thanks to "John P. Speno" <speno@swarthmore.edu> for that special hint
and to Knut.Hellebo@nho.hydro.com for the hint that tcsh may be the problem.

Now my prompt appears with the dxterm most times or shortly after that
and i'm happy with that behaviour again.

