The panics of our 8200 SMP with Digital Unix 3.2C appear
to have gone.
-) We installed firmware rev. 2.2-102 , SROM V1.3
   ** Many Thanks to Matthias Dolder of Digital Switzerland
      how made us aware of this firmware upgrade
-) We installed the patches to Digital Unix 3.2C of 
   october 7 
   ** thanks to Digital Engineering!
The two steps above solved the bulk of problems.
The remaining occasional lock timeouts (with panic) we
avoided by setting
  generic:
    locktimeout=60
into /etc/sysconfigtab  (and rebooting).
After this increasing of the locktimeout from the default of
15 seconds to 60 seconds we run with 6 CPUs again at full
load (both CPU, disk I/O and fddi/nfs) and havent seen
any panics in several days.
Our 8200 has finally gone into production.
Walter Brueckner



