In article <26OCT95.18374670@bureau.ucc.ie>
Niall Madden <scmt6051@bureau.ucc.ie> wrote:
> Hi,
> 
>         I recently tried to up the max number of users on you alpha/osf
> system. However, as I didn't deleted to old OSF-USR licence before adding
> the new one I have problems. The message I get is 
> Combine OSF-USR ASP-IL-1995SEP13-1811 with OSF-USR OSF-BASE-IMPLICIT-USER

> and "delete osf-usr" gives
> Information provided was ambiguous; multiple licenses were found

Well the answer is to be less ambiguous.  From lmf man page:

  delete product [ producer [ authorization ] ]
          Deletes a license from the License Database and the kernel cache.
          Before you issue this command, be sure you have a record of the
          license either in a file on your system or in hardcopy format.


So something like:

lmf> delete OSF-USR DEC OSF-BASE-IMPLICIT-USER

should do the trick.  **NOTE** - you might want to use the issue command 
instead as this allows you to write the license you remove to a file (just in 
case).

i.e.

lmf> issue osf-usr-backup OSF-USR DEC OSF-BASE-IMPLICIT-USER

---
Ewan



