Again, because what's currently on the net is still in Beta test,
we've got to be free to introduce incompatibilities from one test
version to the next.  As with our released binary translation
products, VEST and MX (aka "DECmigrate"), backward compatibility
for programs that you've  translated will be a requirement that we
impose on ourselves for future versions, once we've officially
released this first version.

To date, the interface between an fpx-translated application and the
fpxr runtime module has changed radically several times during 
development. By expiring the current software, including the translated
images, we ensure that we've got breathing room to do it again if
it proves to be necessary.

