If you want to integrate Mailworks, sendmail and MSMAIL, you should take a
look at PMDF (contact sales@innosoft.com).  This product can speak to sendmail
using SMTP (requires TCP/IP on your VMS platform), supporting MIME attachments
EHLO extensions etc.  It can speak to Mailworks either by talking to Message
Router (if you have it), or by emulating the Message Router interface (if
you don't) tricking Mailworks into thinking it's talking to Message Router.

It also has an MSMAIL post office gateway giving mail access (including file
attachments <-> MIME) to that mailer, as well as CCMAIL and others.  It also
contains POP and IMAP servers, allowing you to run PC user agents such as
PINE.  Finally, it has optional X400, fax and API gateways.  Product has superb
reliability, and excellent support.  We use it extensively, and are very
happy with it.

