X-Deja-AN: 117928521
references: <466frl$eop@jaguar.convex.com> <468fe4$hlk@lll-winken.llnl.gov> <469fhb$4to@usenet.pa.dec.com>
organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,vmsnet.alpha


Alpha VMS uses granularity hints for _most_ of the EXEC's nonpaged code and
data. (see the show memory/gh_region display). It uses a combination of 8, 64
and 512 page 'chunks' to make up these regions.

The INSTALL utility also has the capability of installing images into
GH regions (see INSTALL's help on /resident).

The Alpha VMS memory management system services will automatically set GH if
the virtual and physical memory ranges being work with meet the requirements of
GH. The DECwindows server process uses this feature to map things like frame
buffers.

Dave



