organization: ABB Atom Nuclear Fuel
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.sys.dec,comp.unix.osf.osf1

Hi folks!

I had some questions about running Digital Unix on a Multia.
Everything was running OK except for the small 17" screen I got,
and I was completely unable to change the screen size.

I got three responses:
erik@lenatest.rydnet.lysator.liu.se (Erik Persson)
gallatin@isds.Duke.EDU (Andrew Gallatin)
peterm@langmuir.EECS.Berkeley.EDU (Peter Mardahl)

They all either suggested that I change a file:
/var/X11/xdm/Xservers to contain
:0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -terminate -screen0 1280

and/or change some DIP switches on the graphics card.

The answer turned out to be:

There is a small group of jumpers on the Multia motherboard, located
below the PCI slot. Find them and pull every jumper out.
Voila, you now get 1280x1024 @ 72 Hz!

It was not necessary to change anything in /var/X11/xdm/Xservers.

