Keith,

	Cd to /dev and do a ls -al tty0*.  Then type 'mknod tty03 c XX 3',
where XX is the major number of tty00.  

Mine is like this:
crw-------   1 root     sec       24,  2 Oct 12 01:37 tty00
crw-rw-rw-   1 root     system    24,  3 Oct  3 17:33 tty01

and the mknod line would be
mknod tty03 c 24 3


