In article <45htbd$380@news.cc.oberlin.edu>, cjim@ocaxp0.cc.oberlin.edu (Jim Anderson) writes:

>Any hints on dump parameters on a tlz07 on V3.2?

Yes.  None.  If dump behaves correctly, it will detect EOT and ask
for a new tape when it needs one.  And, since the TLZ07 is supported
on V3.2 dump should be able to get the information it needs to make
reasonably accurate estimates (without compression).  Since the compress
ratio can vary greating, it is hard to get good estimates with compression
turned on.

