In article <45iln8$3tc@usenet.pa.dec.com> double@taxe11.tao.dec.com (Double Chiang) writes:

> I read from FAQ for how to rename a bunch file from lower to upper,
> it said you should write a script. like following.

> foreach f (*)
>   mv $f 'echo $f | tr '[a-z]' '[A-Z]''
> end

> but when I tried to execute this script, the shell complain about 
> mv: . No match. 

> What's wrong? my shell is tcsh. Thanks in advance.


The quotes are wrong:
...
>   mv $f 'echo $f | tr '[a-z]' '[A-Z]''
...       ^                            ^

You have to use:
...
    mv $f `echo $f | tr '[a-z]' '[A-Z]'`
...       ^                            ^

Walter
