: Compiling with different optimization levels doesn't help. 

I have experienced this behaviour on more than one machine and have traced
it to:
1) Compiling under NFS (objects going to an NFS mounted disk) and
2) Running programs which expected automatic variables to be 0s.

It doesn't look like #2 applies here since it's the first statement executed.
Does #1 apply ??
