>but only to block areas (thanks, Digital !). This implies
>repartitioning a disk, which will get me stuck (unsuficient backup
>devices available).
>
>Isn't there a way to increase swap space without reformating ?

If you don't have a spare partition, to be used for extra swap space,
the answer is NO.

But you can increase the efficiency of the available swap space by 
removing (or renaming) /sbin/swapdefault and rebooting.  Depending on
how much extra swap space you need, this might solve your problem.  The
implications of this action are described in the swapon man page.

