I made the following guess, and it seems to work on my Alpha 400 4/233.
If some one has better hack, please let me know.

Makefile:
	CFLAGS  = -O -DALPHA -DBSD -DLOCKF

devices.c:
	#ifdef ALPHA
	struct device devices[] = {
	        {'A', "/dev/rfd0a", 0L, 12, 0, (int (*) ()) 0, 80, 2, 18},
	        {'A', "/dev/rfd0a", 0L, 12, 0, (int (*) ()) 0, 80, 2, 9},
	        {'\0', (char *) NULL, 0L, 0, 0, (int (*) ()) 0, 0, 0, 0}
	};
	#endif /* ALPHA */

Good luck,
Jari Vaario




