	Here are some numbers,


	UFS:	theoretical file system size is 1TB, Digital supports max.
		128GB's which is currently max. logical volume size supported
		by LSM. Single file should be able to populate all free space.

	AdvFS:	Current largest theoretical file and file set size is 16TB if
		you can build such a domain. In practise limits come from 
		i/o controllers and volumes you have available.

	LSM:	LSM supports 128 disks in groups, and latest material available
		states that LSM supports max. of 128GB's of space/volume, 
		but this information may be obsolete as I suppose this hasn't
		been updated recently...

	What are the limits you need ?
	
