Hi,

I am looking into ways to automate account generation. On OSF/1
this gets difficult for 2 main resaons:

	a) the passwords are held in /tcb/auth/files
	b) OSF uses dbm style passwd files for fast lookup.

There is an adduser script, but it is interactive and rebuilds
the dbm file every time, which can take quite some time with a huge
passwd file.

We could just add all users to /etc/passwd and then run mkuser, but
we will still have to change each user's passwd in the tcb.

Has anyone done a batch-style user generation program that makes these
easy and fast?

