Jarkko Hietaniemi (Jarkko.Hietaniemi@hut.fi) wrote:
: Does this mean also a new DFS release? Any spec sheets for the new
: DSF releases? For example, will the Digital DFS support ADVfs as the
: native filesystem?

The Digital DCE/DFS product supports UFS and AdvFS now.
The real problem is that Digital does not sell a DFS
product with LFS (Episode) extensions. The implications
of this is that the current DEC release does not support
the more useful administrative facilities available in
DFS:

	fileset replication
	backup (clone) volumes
	full DCE ACL support on files and directories
	ability to interoperate with the bakserver/tcid backup tools 

Hopefully, Digital with either support LFS or will graft the
functionality onto AdvFS in the near future to provide the 
full replication semantics that is useful for large sites that
require that functionality.. 

-- Jim Doyle



