I agree with most of what has been said before however two more points:

1)	Check the defines associated with std1 and std, we had to make a change
from std to std1 in our make files.

2) I was working on OSF2.1 so this may have changed, but watch our for
something like this

void setVal( Int *i)
long l;

...
	setVal( (int*) &l)

We found half of the long was initialised in setVal, but the rest was
rubbish - causig a few problems.

Basically it comes down to longs and pointers are 64 bits which are not the
same size as other data types.

