In article <44prrk$79u@Owl.nstn.ca>, dmarr@office.city.dartmouth.ns.ca
(David Marr) wrote:

> I would like to be able to connect a laser printer with an ethernet port
> to by OSF box.  I have no idea what the printcap entry should look like
> for such a connection.  Any help would be greatly appreciated.

    David -

    I don't know if you got an answer or worked it out for yourself yet,
but here's our printcap entry (subtly modified to prevent spamming) for a
networked HP 4SiMX (text queue):

lp1|1|fred-laser2|HP LaserJet 4 SiMX (remote):\    <- queue names
        :lf=/usr/spool/hp4simx/errors:\   <- directory for error logging
        :lp=:\
        :mx#0:\
        :rm=fred-laser2:\                 <- IP alias of printer
        :rp=text:\                        <- queue name in printer
                                             (printer docs should supply)
        :sd=/usr/spool/hp4simx:           <- directory for spooled files
                                          <- you'll need to mkdir this and
                                          <- the errors directories

    
    On HP 4's with PostScript, PostScript fils are not (well)
auto-recognized; for PostScript, you'd have to set up a separate queue
with

         :rp=raw:\

On some Tektronix color printers we use, the PostScript rp name is PS.

     Hope this helps,

                  Joe Gurman

