Kenny House (house@wrksys.enet.dec.com) wrote:

>     I've been told that the sound of the 'beep' on the AlphaStation 200 and
>     250 can be improved by moving the internal speaker connection from the
>     small sound card (at a four-pin header marked J5) to the Main Logic
>     Board (at a similar four-pin header marked J15).

Success!!!  At least partial....  One correction is that the
speaker-out on the main board is J18 (J15 is the internal SCSI
cable connector).

I've now got a bell that sounds right!  I can control the pitch and
duration through xset, but the volume seems to still be an "all or
nothing" kind of deal.  That's really not such a big deal now since
the beep is at a reasonable level (not nearly as loud as it was
through the sound card).

>     If this is done, you now require external speakers if you want to use
>     the sound card's output.

The sound card still works through the headphones, which is how I
prefer to use it on those rare occasions when I want to use it (all
work and no play, you know....)

Anyway, thanks for the tip!  It has made my "work environment" much
nicer (xbiff was REALLY starting to annoy me).  I highly recommend
this to others with AlphaStations (do you really want to listen to
your sound card through that cheezy speaker anyway???).

